{# summary.md.j2 — the skeleton for notes/summaries/<discipline>/<NNN>-<slug>.md

   One hand-written skeleton owns the entire mechanical surface; a per-family data
   file (notes/data/summaries/<NNN>.md) supplies the prose bodies with quote
   tokens. The renderer (build_summaries.py) composes them from quotes.tsv.

   The canonical surface this template fixes across every page:
   - the title line carries an em dash: `# <NNN> — <Title>`
   - the breadcrumbs link "Family <NNN>" to the family's index page, making the
     summary<->index edge bidirectional (60 index pages already link to the summary)
   - one prose heading set: the 30 distinct strings the hand-written pages carried
     collapse to the canonical sections below, each rendered only when the family
     has a body for it
   - the Sources table is four columns with one separator byte form, and each File
     cell is a markdown link to its file (the cell is both the path and its link)
   - a Bibliography section after Sources (math-cgv.8)

   Every {{ }} slot is a label the renderer supplies. Rendering uses trim_blocks and
   lstrip_blocks, so the {% if %}/{% endif %} and {% for %}/{% endfor %} lines emit
   nothing and the body lines emit verbatim. #}
